          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
          %p
            By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirzebruch-Riemann-Roch+theorem"} Hirzebruch-Riemann-Roch theorem
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dolbeault+operator"} Dolbeault operator
            is the Todd genus (e.g.
            %a{:href => "#Gilkey95"} Gilkey 95, section 5.2
            (more generally so for the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%5Ec+Dirac+operator"} Spin^c Dirac operator
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "genus#LogarithmAndCharacteristicSeries"} characteristic series
            of the Todd genus is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi x
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x \,\mapsto\, \frac{x}{ 1 - e^{-x} }
                  \\,.
          %p
            This means that as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+classes"} Chern classes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_i
            the Todd class starts out as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi td
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 12
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 24
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi deg
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  td
                  \\;=\;
                  1
                  +
                  \\tfrac{1}{2} c_1
                  +
                  \\tfrac{1}{12}
                  \\big(
                  c_1^2 + c_2
                  \\big)
                  +
                  \\tfrac{1}{24}
                  c_1 c_2
                  +
                  \\mathcal{O}(deg \geq 8)
                  \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationBetweenToddClassAndAHatGenus
            Relation between Todd class and
            = succeed "-genus" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A
          %p
            On an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+complex+manifold"} almost complex manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{\mathrm{U}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+class"} Todd class
            coincides with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-hat+genus"} A-hat class
            up to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential"} exponential
            of half the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Td
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Td(M_{\mathrm{U}})
                  \\;=\;
                  \\big(e^{c_1/2} \hat A\big)(M_{\mathrm{U}})
                  \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Freed87"} Freed 87 (1.1.14)
          %p
            In particular, on manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{S\mathrm{U}}
            with
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} SU
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} structure
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1 = 0
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-hat+genus"} A-hat class
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Td
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
